###
title: LDA atoms miss the virial theorem by under 5%
line: $-V/T$ exceeds 2 by 4.9% for hydrogen down to 0.19% for argon, with energies within $5 \times 10^{-7}$ hartree of NIST.
claim: For the neutral atoms $Z = 1$ to 18 in the local density approximation (dftatom, LDA with VWN correlation), the virial ratio $-V/T$ exceeds 2 by between 0.001 and 0.05 (4.9% for hydrogen down to 0.19% for argon), shrinking at every step in $Z$. The same runs reproduce NIST's LDA total energies to within $5 \times 10^{-7}$ hartree on every atom, inside NIST's $10^{-6}$ rounding, so the departure comes from the model.
topic: science
section: atomic structure
reference: NIST Standard Reference Database 141 (Atomic Reference Data for Electronic Structure Calculations, LDA column, lib/nistref.viv) for the total energies; the virial theorem $2T + V = 0$ for Coulomb systems, which density-functional LDA satisfies only up to the correlation functional's departure from homogeneous scaling (Levy and Perdew, Phys. Rev. A 32, 2010 (1985)). dftatom is Certik, Pask and Vackar's code (Comput. Phys. Commun. 184, 1777 (2013)) as ported in ports/dftatom.
scope: Neutral atoms Z = 1 to 18 (hydrogen to argon) in NIST's ground configurations, nonrelativistic LDA with VWN correlation, dftatom's default mesh (6,000 points to 50 bohr) and tolerances. V is everything but the kinetic energy (Hartree, electron-nucleus, exchange-correlation). The expected cause, LDA correlation's departure from homogeneous scaling (Levy and Perdew), is not isolated here by an exchange-only run.
lane: ai
by: claude
cost: fast
###

from ports.dftatom.dftatom import atom_scf, EKIN, ECOUL, EENUC, EXC, ETOT
from nistref import AL_LDA_ETOT, AR_LDA_ETOT, B_LDA_ETOT, BE_LDA_ETOT, C_LDA_ETOT, CL_LDA_ETOT, F_LDA_ETOT, H_LDA_ETOT, HE_LDA_ETOT, LI_LDA_ETOT, MG_LDA_ETOT, N_LDA_ETOT, NA_LDA_ETOT, NE_LDA_ETOT, O_LDA_ETOT, P_LDA_ETOT, S_LDA_ETOT, SI_LDA_ETOT

N_ATOMS: Int = 18
NIST_ETOT = [H_LDA_ETOT, HE_LDA_ETOT, LI_LDA_ETOT, BE_LDA_ETOT, B_LDA_ETOT, C_LDA_ETOT, N_LDA_ETOT, O_LDA_ETOT, F_LDA_ETOT, NE_LDA_ETOT, NA_LDA_ETOT, MG_LDA_ETOT, AL_LDA_ETOT, SI_LDA_ETOT, P_LDA_ETOT, S_LDA_ETOT, CL_LDA_ETOT, AR_LDA_ETOT]
#: dftatom's defaults (ports/dftatom/atom.viv)
R_MIN = 1.0e-7
R_MAX = 50.0
MESH_A = 2.7e6
MESH_N: Int = 6000
C_LIGHT = 137.0359895
REIGEN_EPS = 1.0e-10
REIGEN_MAX: Int = 100
MIX_EPS = 5.0e-9
MIX_ALPHA = 0.5
MIX_MAX: Int = 200

virial_dev = zeros(N_ATOMS)
nist_err = zeros(N_ATOMS)
all_converged = true
for zi to N_ATOMS {
    d, conv, its = atom_scf(zi + 1, false, R_MIN, R_MAX, MESH_A, MESH_N, C_LIGHT, REIGEN_EPS, REIGEN_MAX, MIX_EPS, MIX_ALPHA, MIX_MAX, true)
    if not conv {
        all_converged = false
    }
    pot = d.energies[ECOUL] + d.energies[EENUC] + d.energies[EXC]
    virial_dev[zi] = -pot / d.energies[EKIN] - 2.0
    nist_err[zi] = abs(d.energies[ETOT] - NIST_ETOT[zi])
}
show virial_dev
show nist_err
worst_virial = max(abs(virial_dev))
worst_nist = max(nist_err)
show worst_virial
show worst_nist
show all_converged
virial_hydrogen = virial_dev[0]
virial_argon = virial_dev[N_ATOMS - 1]
show virial_hydrogen
show virial_argon
#: NIST SRD 141 rounds its energies to 1e-6 hartree
NIST_ROUNDING = 1.0e-6

#: the figure: the excess of -V/T over 2, in percent, for Z = 1 .. 18
PERCENT = 100.0
fg_z = zeros(N_ATOMS)
for fg_k to N_ATOMS {
    fg_z[fg_k] = fg_k + 1.0
}
figure("Virial ratio of LDA atoms", "atomic number Z", "(-V/T - 2), %")
yscale("log")
plot(fg_z, abs(virial_dev) * PERCENT, "LDA, dftatom")
style("LDA, dftatom", "s1 circle")

test "every atom converged" {
    assert_true(all_converged)
}
test "-V/T exceeds 2 by between 0.001 and 0.05 on every atom" {
    for zi to N_ATOMS {
        assert_gt(virial_dev[zi], 0.001)
        assert_lt(virial_dev[zi], 0.05)
    }
}
test "the excess shrinks at every step in Z" {
    for zi from 1 to N_ATOMS {
        assert_lt(virial_dev[zi], virial_dev[zi - 1])
    }
}
test "total energies within 5e-7 hartree of NIST, inside its 1e-6 rounding" {
    assert_lt(worst_nist, 5.0e-7)
    assert_lt(worst_nist, NIST_ROUNDING)
}

